+Missing duration, token, or model telemetry also remains `unknown`. Mission
+Control must not infer observations from requested values or convert missing
+data to zero.
+
+Cost is reported more precisely, because "no number" has more than one cause:
+
+| `cost_status` | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `reported` | The runtime declared a total itself (Claude `total_cost_usd`) |
+| `derived` | Citadel summed that runtime's own per-model components (Claude `modelUsage[*].costUSD`) |
+| `unavailable` | A trusted observation came from a runtime that declares no cost at all (Codex) |
+| `unknown` | Telemetry is missing, untrusted, or names a cost source Citadel cannot attest |
+
+Derivation only ever sums cost the runtime itself stated. A partial breakdown is
+refused rather than understated, cost is never priced from tokens, and the cost
+source must belong to the closed provenance registry in `executor-profiles.js`
+before any amount is shown. A branch with a cost always carries `reported` or
+`derived`; `unavailable` and `unknown` always carry a null cost.

